# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored - never commit a real key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Fill in whichever drivers you plan to run. Paste keys with no quotes around
# them: a key copied out of a document carries curly quotes, the shell keeps
# those as literal characters, and both drivers refuse such a key on sight.

# --driver gemini. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# NOTE: the free tier allows 20 requests per day for gemini-3.6-flash and one
# agent run costs six to eight, so a five-scenario sweep with three repeats -
# about 106 requests - needs billing enabled.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --driver cerebras. Get a key at https://cloud.cerebras.ai
#
# The free tier allows 2,400 requests and 1M tokens per day, which covers a full
# sweep several times over. The binding limit is five requests per minute, the
# same as Gemini's free tier, so runs still spend time waiting out throttling.
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# The model under test is a command-line flag, not an environment variable:
#
#   arena run --driver cerebras --model gpt-oss-120b
#
# Each driver defaults to its own, so --model is only needed to override one.
#
# NOTE: gemini-3.1-pro-preview is documented as prone to ignoring custom tool
# definitions in favour of bash. Use gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools if you
# switch to Pro, and record which variant produced your results.
